{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/529685-plot-twist-ideas","id":529685,"title":"Plot Twist Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-27T01:51:27-07:00","id":529685,"title":"Plot Twist Ideas","content":"Hi folks, I'm running a Vampire 2.0 campaign set in Manhattan and part of the background was that the local Vampires have been very thorough on wiping out the Werewolf population in Manhattan. My original idea was it was simply a turf war over Central Park. Vampires seeing it as prime feeding real estate and the local werewolves trying to keep hold of their territory in the park plus a powerful locus there. <br /> <br /> Now though, the players have really gotten into the idea of discovering the history behind the eradication policy and want to find out why it came about. Now, I could still run with the idea of it mainly being a mere turf war, but since the players are into it, does anyone have a nice idea as to why the Vampires of Manhattan have been offing the local werewolf population to replace the original idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T02:02:45-07:00","id":529705,"title":"","content":"Why is Central Park prime feeding real estate? People don't go there at night, and when they do and get attacked, it's a big deal and makes the news. It's one of those places where it'll definitely get televised, and definitely advertised to people as a big problem. Feeding in Central Park is a terrible idea for multiple Kindred. Maybe one. Why would Uratha care about that, anyway?<br /> <br /> I advocate making it more interesting. Maybe the most influential Pack in Manhattan (Not a whole lot of space there for a ton of different packs...) might have a Totem that demands some kind of animosity towards Kindred. Maybe the Kindred in power have somehow become influenced by a Spirit Court hostile to the Uratha in Manhattan, and want them driven out of the borough. Maybe there's a creepy Idigam underneath Manhattan that's chosen a high up Vampire as its Herald somehow, and wants the Uratha cleared out of the borough so it can go about its business undisturbed.<br /> <br /> If you want the 'fault' as it were on the side of the Werewolves, maybe there's a Lodge of Iron Masters that makes a specific policy out of hunting the Kindred as a sacred prey, or maybe one of the packs lost a member or two to feeding, and the Uratha decided that extermination was the only acceptable answer to dealing with this parasite.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a spirit court that's gotten Magath'd by funky Essence thanks to a Kindred ritual or accident, and they subtly make it easier for vampires to feed in the borough so they can generate more of their preferred Essence. The Uratha noticed that this was happening and decided that it was no good at all, and you have the present situation.<br /> <br /> Those are some general reasons. If you have any major players outlined then we might be able to give specific ideas based on that.<br /> <br /> P.S. I'd love to hear about your New York setting if you're willing to share, either here or in PMs!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T02:26:00-07:00","id":529723,"title":"","content":"Ah, see, I went with the nWoD idea that the WoD is a shittier version of our world so a lot of homeless use Central Park as a place to sleep the night away (though currently its a bit thin on the ground with feeding targets thanks to a nasty winter, so most homeless have retreated underground.) Also, the police presence and media coverage are a lot less than they are in reality thanks to a couple Invictus working to keep it that way.<br /> <br /> Also, it doesn't have to be the Uratha at fault, something nasty to pin on a vampiric mover and shaker in the city would be fine too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the New York City setting, I haven't actually developed much of it yet beyond the basic beats. Manhattan has an Invictus prince, so its run fairly generic to the setting. The Carthian leader is nutty and wants war (something the players haven't cottoned onto yet even though he's been using them to attack the Invictus). There are near no Werewolves to be found on Manhattan due to the aforementioned eradication policy. Gangrel as a clan claim the subway system and the Nosferatu claim the Sewers and below and both have been jabbing at one another for complete control of the underground of Manhattan.<br /> <br /> This is mainly because I originally developed Manhattan as a Mage setting and while I've been running a campaign, my players asked if I could run another game so we could get more play time in (and I did want to try out second edition since I hadn't before that). Thus I've only had three sessions in Vampire so far and I've mainly used it to introduce them to the rules and the vampire condition.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, that could be a nice idea. Didn't spot your mention of the Idigam before my reply. Having the Carthian Leader being influenced by an Idigam as the reason for his nuttier warmongering could be a nice idea to play on. I could make him the original instigator of the eradication policy, and now that the Uratha are taken care of, his &quot;master&quot; could be the one trying to get him to make war within the covenants to further its own aims (ie. removing threats/rivals within the city.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 05-27-2015, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T02:53:39-07:00","id":529727,"title":"","content":"I'm not gonna lie, I was playing with an idea like that myself. I simultaneously wanted to pay homage to and avoid the whole &quot;Tzimisce antediluvian under New York&quot; thing from oWoD, so I was gonna have it be an Idigam that may have coalesced in the presence of a Kindred feeding frenzy or something else fucked up like that.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the New York write up in <i>Damnation City </i>mentions that Kindred just... disappear here, sometimes. It's the concrete jungle, man. Could play with that.<br /> <br /> On top of that, I <i>believe </i>the Neglatu writeup mentions that they infest New York's Sewers... Maybe a connection? Some more stuff to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T03:13:24-07:00","id":529731,"title":"","content":"Could be that there's a Wyrm's Nest in Central Park. While the Ordo may or may not be influential in your story, perhaps there's an elder that influence with the Prince. A favor for the Prince years ago may have paved the way for the Kindred to slowly begin pushing the wolves out of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}